window.receiveProjectSource({"path": ".docs/specs/ingest/BRD-data-ingestion.md", "lines": ["# BRD \u2014 First-Party Customer Data Ingestion", "", "| | |", "|---|---|", "| **Status** | Draft \u2014 errata pass 2026-07-22: aligned to the ingestion design and dated STATE entries (engine-path framing \u00a71.1, quarantine zones \u00a73.0/\u00a74.8, identity-field split \u00a74, latency classes \u00a74.9); pass-5 alignment same-day (FR-1.5/FR-4.5 two-grain intake timing \u00a74.7, FR-1.6 declared scan policy \u00a74.8, FR-4.9 minimal survivor set \u00a74.12); errata pass 2026-07-24 (product-owner approved, STATE): FR-5.3/FR-5.4/OD-7 aligned to the decided synthesis serialization contract (design \u00a74.17), FR-3.7/NFR-2 model tier \u2192 dated verified allowlist pointer, FR-2.5 registered-format scope, NFR-1 declared-serialization-key sentence; 2026-07-26 DAT-7968 sync: bounded hot-store field, deterministic finalist selection, GovCloud-scale and metadata-guided artifact-query gates |", "| **Date** | 2026-07-14 (errata 2026-07-22, 2026-07-24, 2026-07-26) |", "| **Owner** | TBD |", "| **Program** | Government intelligence-layer expansion |", "| **Related** | `STATE.md` (decisions log), `govt-workstreams.xlsx` (workstream inventory), Investigate Mode BRD (separate, forthcoming) |", "", "---", "", "## 1. Business context & problem statement", "", "Polaris today ingests one kind of data: third-party news and article content,", "processed by the Datalake2 pipeline (event extraction \u2192 Event Synthesis", "Service \u2192 `event_synth.source_events` in accelerate), which feeds the Signal", "and Pattern engines. The government and government-adjacent segment this", "program targets is different: **customers with large first-party data", "holdings and no intelligence layer above them**. Polaris is that layer. These", "customers supply their own data \u2014 streams and bulk drops whose type, format,", "and semantics vary wildly from one client to the next, at volumes ranging", "from gigabytes per day to a stated future extreme of petabyte-class per hour", "(video-dominated). LLNL is one anchor prospect in this segment, not the", "driver; the capability set below serves the segment as a whole.", "", "Three business problems drive this BRD:", "", "1. **Revenue is gated on ingestion.** The engines only see what reaches", "   `source_events`. Without a first-party intake path, the platform cannot", "   serve customers whose data is their own.", "2. **Per-client onboarding cost is a sales-cycle constraint.** If every new", "   customer's data formats require weeks of engineering, deal velocity and", "   margin both suffer. Onboarding a new client's data must be primarily a", "   configuration exercise, assisted by LLM agents that identify the data's", "   shape and propose the pipeline configuration.", "3. **The government boundary changes the mechanics.** Extraction runs on", "   cheap OpenAI calls today; inside a GovCloud boundary all LLM calls must", "   run in-boundary on Bedrock (Claude at Sonnet 4.5 tier and below) with", "   Titan V2 or in-VPC embeddings (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-10 Bedrock", "   findings; 2026-07-14 embeddings strategy). Every artifact must carry", "   provenance and security labels for chain-of-custody lineage (ACC-5) and", "   record-level access control (ACC-2).", "", "An existing cleanse-and-persist pipeline design by our AWS Solutions", "Architect (Jason Steen) is prior art: its flow logic (cleanse \u2192 persist) is", "expected to survive, but it is PGSQL-backed and the storage target changes to", "the settled three-store map (Section 6).", "", "## 2. Goals / non-goals", "", "### Goals", "", "- Ingest first-party customer data of arbitrary format, per client, with a", "  versioned provenance envelope on every item.", "- Identify each new data source's shape with LLM-agent assistance and", "  configure the per-client pipeline without per-client code forks.", "- Extract entities (canonical and soft), events, and other per-client", "  artifact shapes, using the in-boundary LLM path in government", "  deployments.", "- Ingest and extract from image and video sources on day 1, alongside text.", "- Persist metadata for all source data; persist the source data itself as", "  evidence per source-type policy.", "- Synthesize events at scale on a horizontally scalable write path whose", "  concurrency strategy can vary per stream.", "- Keep event data flowing into `event_synth.source_events` under its", "  existing contract, extended additively and never forked (STATE", "  2026-07-19 \u2014 extend, don't fork the event type), so the existing", "  Signal/Pattern engine path keeps consuming.", "- Support multi-tenant operation everywhere, including government", "  deployments.", "", "### Non-goals", "", "- **Signal Engine / Pattern Engine rework.** They keep consuming", "  `source_events` under the existing, additively extended contract", "  (FR-6.1). The push-flow pivot (SIG-1), the Pattern Engine build (PAT-1),", "  and how engines/agents consume first-party artifacts (the Apollo", "  engagement PRD) are separate workstreams.", "- **Investigate Mode specification.** It gets its own BRD. Here it is a", "  downstream consumer whose query-tool needs shape the persistence and", "  indexing requirements (FR-6.3).", "- **Final hot-store product commitment.** The bake-off structure, field,", "  and pre-registered criteria are recorded in Section 6; running the", "  evaluation and making the final call stays with the storage-architecture", "  workstream (DATA-3).", "- **Extreme-tier build-out on day 1.** SETTLED (STATE 2026-07-14): design", "  the shape to scale; size fleets for the tier actually sold.", "- **Classified or cross-domain data handling.** The government boundary in", "  scope is unclassified/CUI (information-boundary decision gate DG-1).", "", "## 3. Personas & consumers", "", "| Who | Relationship to ingestion |", "|---|---|", "| **Customer data producer** (mission systems, sensors, business systems) | Delivers streams and bulk drops, or grants pull access to a customer-owned store; owns the source archive referenced for large payloads. |", "| **Polaris onboarding engineer** | Runs agent-assisted shape identification, reviews and activates per-client pipeline configuration. |", "| **Signal/Pattern engines** | Consume `source_events` under the existing contract, additively extended (FR-3.3/FR-6.1) \u2014 the primary automated consumer. Their AI judgment layers additionally retrieve datasets explicitly approved as Signal/Pattern judgment context (FR-6.6). |", "| **Investigate Mode agents** (future, own BRD) | Query the full ingested corpus by type, time, entity, client, ingest run, and label; require the indexing surface this BRD specifies. |", "| **Compliance / audit reviewer** | Walks lineage from any derived artifact back to the source item and its markings; verifies handling rules were applied. |", "| **Platform operator** | Monitors throughput, funnel ratios, DLQs, and per-stage cost; scales fleets per tier sold. |", "", "## 4. Functional requirements", "", "### 4.1 Ingestion", "", "- **FR-1.1** The system shall accept first-party data per client through", "  both delivery directions: customer **push** to Polaris-managed intake", "  endpoints/buckets, and Polaris **pull** from customer-owned stores. Both", "  are required capabilities (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14, OD-6).", "- **FR-1.2** The system shall support **bulk/backfill intake** \u2014 historical", "  archive drops such as bulk object-store transfers \u2014 as a first-class", "  intake mode riding the same envelope and pipeline as streams, with", "  throughput isolation so a backfill never starves live processing (STATE", "  2026-07-15).", "- **FR-1.3** The system shall move bulk payloads as parallel S3 object", "  writes, with a control plane carrying envelopes and references: a stream", "  backbone \u2014 leaning Kafka/MSK under the open-source deployability rule", "  (Section 6), with final product selection at implementation \u2014 plus SQS", "  work queues that distribute AI-processing tasks to workers with per-task", "  acknowledgement, retry, and dead-letter handling (SETTLED shape \u2014 STATE", "  2026-07-14, OD-2; architecture owned by the durable streaming and replay", "  workstream, DATA-2).", "- **FR-1.4** Queues and streams shall carry **pointers only** \u2014 S3 URI plus", "  envelope \u2014 never payload bytes. A worker processing an image or video", "  receives a reference and reads the payload from object storage.", "- **FR-1.5** The system shall stamp every accepted item with the versioned", "  provenance envelope \u2014 source/provenance, security labels, the distinct", "  identity fields (FR-1.7), content type, content hash \u2014 **at two grains**", "  (design \u00a74.7, aligned 2026-07-22): the **delivery unit's** envelope and", "  identity at the transport edge, from delivery config alone; the", "  **record's** envelope and identity at post-scan normalization, when", "  accepted bytes are first parsed \u2014 no record-grain identity exists before", "  that stage, and intake receipts are unit-grain until it completes.", "  Payloads land first in an **ephemeral quarantine zone**, never directly", "  in evidence storage: only items accepted by validation, scanning, and", "  triage are promoted into the immutable evidence lake. Items that fail", "  shall be quarantined with a recorded reason \u2014 never silently dropped;", "  quarantined bytes expire at a configured TTL while the quarantine record", "  and accounting persist (STATE 2026-07-18 quarantine landing zone;", "  ingestion design \u00a73.0/\u00a74.8).", "- **FR-1.6** Customer-supplied payloads (files, images, video) shall be", "  scanned for malware in the in-flight triage tier (DATA-10) \u2014 against the", "  quarantine zone, before promotion to evidence and before any extraction", "  touches them; items failing the scan, and unscannable items (fail-closed),", "  shall be quarantined with a recorded reason (STATE 2026-07-15; ingestion", "  design \u00a73.0/\u00a74.8). Scanning follows a per-source **declared, versioned", "  scan policy** (design \u00a74.8, aligned 2026-07-22): required engine set,", "  timeout and aggregation rules (most-severe-wins), and \u2014 where a source", "  declares it at onboarding \u2014 an over-cap posture of structure validation", "  plus sandboxed decode whose verdict is recorded as a distinct", "  policy-scoped class, never conflated with a signature-clean verdict; no", "  byte is promoted without its declared policy's recorded verdict. This is", "  the data-plane counterpart", "  of the software-supply-chain workstream (ENV-6), which covers only", "  software entering the boundary.", "- **FR-1.7** Every ingested item shall carry **distinct identity fields,", "  never one overloaded id** (supersedes this BRD's earlier single", "  `ingest_trace_id` \u2014 STATE 2026-07-19 identity split; ingestion design", "  \u00a74): `tenant_id` (the platform client id \u2014 this BRD's `client_id` \u2014", "  taken from authenticated intake, never payload metadata), `operation_id`", "  (nullable client-defined operational grouping; renamed from `mission_id`", "  for segment neutrality), `source_system_id`, the source record id +", "  version, `ingest_batch_id` (bulk/backfill run grouping), and a", "  per-attempt `trace_id` for **observability only** \u2014 never identity,", "  scoping, or a destruction target.", "- **FR-1.8** The system shall support multi-tenant operation, including in", "  GovCloud deployments: isolation enforced through `client_id` plus the", "  platform's access-control layers, with per-tenant encryption keys where", "  warranted. Dedicated single-customer deployments remain a contract-level", "  option, not an architectural assumption (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14;", "  supersedes the earlier single-tenant working assumption).", "- **FR-1.9** The system shall process duplicate deliveries of the same item", "  idempotently: redelivery shall not produce duplicate downstream artifacts.", "- **FR-1.10** The system shall isolate clients logically: one client's", "  configuration errors, malformed data, or volume spikes shall not degrade", "  another client's pipeline.", "- **FR-1.11** The extraction work queues shall enforce **per-client quotas", "  and priority**, grounded in the `client_id` tag, so no client's volume", "  can starve another client's processing (STATE 2026-07-15).", "- **FR-1.12** The system shall apply backpressure and dead-letter handling", "  at each stage, with operator-visible queue and DLQ depth.", "- **FR-1.13** The system shall retain enough intake history to replay", "  accepted items through the pipeline without creating duplicates. Routine", "  historical re-runs are not a committed requirement; the door stays open", "  (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-10).", "", "### 4.2 Data-shape identification & client onboarding", "", "This is the capability this BRD owns that exists nowhere in the platform", "today (client onboarding & data-shape identification, DATA-12).", "", "- **FR-2.1** Given samples from a new client feed, the system shall produce", "  an LLM-agent-assisted **data-shape profile**: format, structure/schema,", "  field semantics, modality, and volume characteristics.", "- **FR-2.2** From the shape profile, the system shall propose a **per-client", "  pipeline configuration**: parsers/normalizers, field mappings, extraction", "  prompts or skills, entity-resolution posture, per-source-type", "  evidence/retention policy, funnel/retention ratios, and the agent-facing", "  type, dataset and relationship registry entries that make the shape", "  queryable (design \u00a74.5, \u00a74.6, \u00a74.14) \u2014 expressed as reviewable", "  configuration, not code.", "- **FR-2.3** Agent-proposed configuration shall follow a", "  **propose-for-approval** model: an operator reviews, edits, approves, and", "  versions each configuration before activation, and activation is recorded", "  with actor and timestamp (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14, OD-4). The first", "  version of the \"onboarding agent\" may literally be an engineer driving an", "  interactive AI coding session; productized automation comes later.", "- **FR-2.4** Before a client pipeline goes live, the proposed configuration", "  shall run sample data through a **sandboxed dry-run mode**; a human shall", "  review extraction quality; only then may the approved configuration advance", "  to the bounded production canary (STATE 2026-07-15). For sources using", "  active platform types, the target-deployment dry-run stops before canonical", "  publication and the retrieval proof runs after final catalog currency", "  activation under the real consumers (design \u00a74.6). When the later per-client", "  type-registration path is required, a separately approved isolated workspace may also activate", "  the proposed type and run its example typed requests/eval triples against", "  sandbox-published rows before production approval (design \u00a74.14; Platform", "  Retrieval PRD \u00a78.10).", "- **FR-2.5** Onboarding a new feed **within a registered format** on a", "  supported method shall not require a code deploy (errata 2026-07-24: a", "  format with **no registered parser** is a reviewed extension shipped as a", "  platform release \u2014 design \u00a74.14\u2013\u00a74.16 \u2014 not configuration). New", "  modalities are platform builds (multi-modal ingestion adapters", "  workstream, DATA-4); everything within a supported modality **and", "  registered format** is configuration.", "- **FR-2.6** Funnel and retention ratios shall be per-client configuration,", "  not architecture (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14; the in-flight triage and", "  reduction tier is owned by DATA-10).", "- **FR-2.7** The system shall record per-client onboarding elapsed time and", "  engineering touch points so onboarding cost is measurable against the", "  ramp target in NFR-6.", "", "### 4.3 Extraction", "", "- **FR-3.1** The system shall extract entity mentions and resolve them", "  against the platform entity registry: link to a canonical entity on match;", "  mint or link a **soft entity** on no-match where the client's", "  configuration allows it (registry mechanics owned by the soft-entity", "  registry workstream, ENT-1; person entities by ENT-2). Today the entity", "  bridge (`ent.entities`) accepts only canonical", "  corp/market/industry/business/brand rows, so both workstreams are hard", "  prerequisites.", "- **FR-3.2** Per-client entity posture (canonical-only, soft-permitted,", "  fuzzy thresholds) shall be pipeline configuration (see FR-2.2).", "- **FR-3.3** The system shall extract events from accepted items and", "  normalize them into the platform raw-event shape consumed by event", "  synthesis. Events remain a first-class artifact and may gain fields.", "- **FR-3.4** Extraction shall produce **typed entity-to-entity relationship", "  records (edges)** (relationship edges & graph retrieval workstream, DATA-11)", "  alongside entities and events. Each edge shall carry: a", "  relationship type, an evidence reference (the event or source item", "  asserting it), a confidence score, the FR-1.7 identity fields", "  (`tenant_id`/`client_id`; `operation_id` and `ingest_batch_id` where", "  present), and", "  security labels inherited from its evidence \u2014 a relationship derived from", "  restricted material is itself restricted. The edge model shall support", "  node-merge redirects so that when the soft-entity registry (ENT-1) or", "  entity resolution at scale (ENT-3) merges two entities, existing edges", "  re-point cleanly (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-15 relationship decision:", "  relationships as data now, graph engine deferred).", "- **FR-3.5** The system shall support per-client artifact shapes beyond", "  events. Non-event artifacts may stay intentionally loosely typed at", "  runtime, protected by first-class platform guardrails \u2014 validation,", "  provenance, security labels \u2014 rather than a rigid global schema; agentic", "  system design is expected to help handle per-client shapes (DIRECTION", "  SET \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14, OD-1; formalization owned by the domain artifact", "  ontology workstream, DATA-9 \u2014 see Open decisions).", "- **FR-3.6** The system shall extract from image and video sources using", "  deterministic frame sampling feeding vision models: hosted vision models", "  in commercial deployments; Nova-class or self-hosted in-VPC vision models", "  in GovCloud (STATE 2026-07-14 \u2014 day-1 scope).", "- **FR-3.7** In government deployments, all extraction LLM calls shall run", "  in-boundary on Bedrock, restricted to **FedRAMP-authorized models per the", "  program's dated verified GovCloud allowlist** (STATE \u2014 last verified", "  2026-07-21, which found 4.6-family Claude models listed; the exact", "  effective set is the standing in-account check, ENV-3 \u2014 never a hardcoded", "  model name in this BRD). No LLM or embedding traffic shall leave the", "  boundary. *(Errata 2026-07-24: replaced the stale \"Sonnet 4.5 tier and", "  below\" constant.)*", "- **FR-3.8** The embedding provider shall be **per-deployment", "  configuration** behind a provider abstraction: commercial deployments stay", "  on OpenAI text-embedding-3-large for now; GovCloud deployments use Titan", "  V2 or an in-VPC embedder. There is no global re-embedding migration:", "  vectors from different models are incomparable and data never crosses the", "  boundary, so cross-boundary consistency buys nothing, and a full", "  commercial re-embed is cost plus likely retrieval-quality regression", "  (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14 embeddings strategy).", "- **FR-3.9** Vector storage shall be dimension-flexible (the current corpus", "  uses 3072-dimension vectors; other providers differ), and similarity", "  thresholds shall be recalibrated per embedding model rather than assumed", "  portable.", "- **FR-3.10** Embedding storage on the master-data corpora that customers", "  may consume inside their deployments (news, corporations, people,", "  businesses, industries) shall be **multi-model**: a side structure keyed", "  by (object, embedding model) rather than a single hardcoded vector", "  column. Titan V2 vectors shall be generated centrally \u2014 commercial-region", "  Bedrock offers Titan \u2014 for corpora flagged as gov-shippable, at flagging", "  time, not for the whole corpus by default. Shipping master data into a", "  deployment ships the vectors matching that deployment's embedding model", "  (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14 master-data embeddings).", "- **FR-3.11** Every extracted artifact shall record the model identifier", "  and version that produced it and an extraction confidence.", "- **FR-3.12** The system shall emit per-item, per-stage extraction cost", "  telemetry (tokens, calls, unit cost) attributable to client and feed.", "", "### 4.4 Persistence & evidence", "", "- **FR-4.1** The system shall persist metadata for every item accepted into", "  the pipeline: envelope fields (including the FR-1.7 identity set),", "  content hash, size, timestamps, and processing disposition. Quarantine", "  outcomes persist as **records** \u2014 scan/triage verdicts with rule and", "  engine versions, plus any operator dispositions \u2014 while quarantined", "  **bytes** expire at TTL (ingestion design \u00a73.0/\u00a74.8). For data dropped by", "  in-flight triage/reduction at high volume tiers (DATA-10), the system", "  shall persist aggregate accounting \u2014 counts, time windows, and the triage", "  rule versions applied \u2014 sufficient to state what was dropped and why.", "- **FR-4.2** The system shall retain the source payload itself as evidence,", "  stored immutably with its content hash, according to an", "  **evidence/retention policy defined per source type** (video vs news", "  articles vs client-specific structured data), configured at client", "  onboarding (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14, OD-3).", "- **FR-4.3** Source data shall NOT be modeled as documents the way current", "  news/article data is (`doc.documents` is not the target). Evidence lives", "  in the lake keyed by envelope identity.", "- **FR-4.4** For raw video, the system shall reference-don't-copy: persist", "  URI plus content hash pointing into the customer's archive, plus short", "  evidence clips around detections (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14).", "  Evidence-clip policy is the dominant retained volume and requires customer", "  sign-off as part of the per-source-type policy (FR-4.2).", "- **FR-4.5** Every persisted artifact \u2014 source metadata, evidence object,", "  extracted entity link, relationship edge, extracted event, per-client", "  artifact \u2014 shall carry", "  the source-item identity minted at intake (`source_item_id`, claimed at", "  post-scan normalization per the FR-1.5 two-grain timing, plus the", "  FR-1.7 identity fields, with field-level provenance per the ingestion", "  design \u00a73.5) so lineage can be walked in both directions (lineage", "  workstream, ACC-5). The per-attempt observability `trace_id` is never", "  the lineage key.", "- **FR-4.6** Security labels from the envelope shall be stamped onto every", "  derived artifact at write time (label semantics owned by the security", "  markings and handling-rules workstream, DATA-8; this pipeline is the write", "  path that must apply them).", "- **FR-4.7** Storage placement shall follow the three-store map in", "  Section 6: object lake for immutable retained truth including evidence;", "  PostgreSQL as the system of record (lineage relationships and the", "  row-level-security floor for access control \u2014 not replaceable); hot", "  analytical store per the selection recorded in Section 6", "  (storage-architecture workstream, DATA-3).", "- **FR-4.8** AI spend, storage, and throughput shall be metered per client", "  and per ingest run \u2014 attributed via `client_id` plus `operation_id` /", "  `ingest_batch_id` (FR-1.7) \u2014", "  extending the platform's existing append-only LLM-usage accounting and", "  its attribution-ID contract. Metering shall be billing-grade: it feeds", "  multi-tenant pricing (STATE 2026-07-15).", "- **FR-4.9** All data attributable to a `client_id` shall be identifiable", "  and destructible, with evidence of destruction produced; `operation_id`", "  (and `ingest_batch_id` for batch runs) additionally enables destruction", "  scoped to a single operation or ingest run \u2014 the observability", "  `trace_id` is never a destruction target (FR-1.7). A **minimal,", "  content-free survivor set** is inherent in this requirement (aligned", "  2026-07-22, design \u00a74.12): the destruction evidence itself must", "  survive, and data-minimized audit/accounting records (aggregate", "  accounting, attributed dispositions, billing-grade metering per FR-4.8)", "  survive per an explicit exemption list owned by the retention and", "  tiering policy workstream (DATA-7) \u2014 which also defines permitted", "  surviving fields and their minimization. Who may authorize", "  destruction follows", "  the same workstream (DATA-7) (STATE 2026-07-15).", "", "### 4.5 Event synthesis", "", "- **FR-5.1** Extracted events shall flow through the existing Event", "  Synthesis Service dedup/merge decision pipeline (create / merge / link /", "  duplicate / ambiguous) into `event_synth.source_events`, with entity links", "  in `source_event_entities`.", "- **FR-5.2** The synthesis write path shall scale horizontally \u2014 no global", "  single writer. Today the service is globally serialized (a single replica", "  consuming one FIFO group), a hard ceiling at first-party volume", "  (scale-out owned by the event-synthesis writer sharding workstream,", "  DATA-5).", "- **FR-5.3** The synthesis write path shall serialize by **declared", "  serialization domain**: the merge scope (tenant/platform \u00d7 operation or", "  standing) by default, with finer per-source/per-event-type **declared", "  serialization keys** under the identity rule (design \u00a74.17). *(Supersedes", "  the 2026-07-14 per-stream concurrency-strategy selection \u2014 STATE", "  2026-07-23/24 resolved one strategy: serialize-by-routing with a leased,", "  SoR-fenced commit; optimistic-with-repair rejected. This FR records the", "  supersession explicitly.)*", "- **FR-5.4** The serialization contract is testable and stronger than the", "  superseded \"bounded duplicate tolerance\": **zero duplicate canonical", "  events from concurrent resolution** (per-lane serialization + the", "  retrieval-closure invariant), and the idempotency and crash-recovery", "  guarantees (per-operation ledger identities, per-operation commit", "  markers) hold under sharding, so replay remains safe (design \u00a74.17).", "- **FR-5.5** Dedup quality at volume \u2014 candidate generation, thresholds,", "  evaluation, operator correction \u2014 is owned by the cross-source semantic", "  dedup workstream (DATA-6) and is a dependency, not re-scoped here.", "", "### 4.6 Downstream contracts", "", "- **FR-6.1** Event data shall keep flowing into `event_synth.source_events`", "  under its existing contract, **extended additively, never forked** \u2014", "  mission/investigative fields (`operation_id`, security labels,", "  source-item links, entity links) are additive and nullable (STATE", "  2026-07-19; F-ING-11 in the ingestion design). Reworking the engines", "  stays a non-goal, but the engine path is **not \"unchanged\"** (corrected", "  2026-07-22 \u2014 this FR's earlier wording was stale per ingestion design", "  \u00a71.1): some ingested items become signals, some feed the L3/L4 judgment", "  layers as reference context (FR-6.6), and events gain fields; that", "  consumption design is owned by the Apollo engagement PRD.", "- **FR-6.2** Entity links shall resolve for both canonical and soft entities", "  once the soft-entity registry (ENT-1) exists; promotion/merge re-pointing", "  follows that workstream's semantics.", "- **FR-6.3** Every persisted artifact class (source metadata, evidence", "  reference, entity, relationship edge, event, per-client artifact) shall be", "  queryable by type,", "  time range, entity, client, operation (`operation_id`), ingest batch", "  (`ingest_batch_id`), security label, and source-item identity", "  (FR-1.7). This is the indexing surface Investigate Mode's query", "  tools will consume \u2014 served by the hot-store query projection (Section 6);", "  the tools themselves are out of scope here.", "- **FR-6.4** The query surface for Investigate Mode tools and", "  judgment-layer context shall include **relationship retrieval**:", "  neighborhood expansion and path queries over the edge records (FR-3.4),", "  one to a few hops, honoring the same access-control enforcement as all", "  other retrieval. Recursive SQL and hot-store joins suffice at day-1", "  tiers; the graph-engine question is deferred (Section 6.2; STATE", "  2026-07-15).", "- **FR-6.5** Retrieval paths over ingested data shall enforce access control", "  at query time: security labels present and indexed so record-level", "  enforcement (the ABAC workstream, ACC-2) applies on retrieval, not by", "  filtering results afterward.", "- **FR-6.6** Ingested datasets carrying the onboarding-approved use", "  **`signal_pattern_judgment_eligible`** shall be retrievable as supplemental", "  evaluation context by the Signal/Pattern engines' AI judgment layers", "  (L3/L4). This use is independent of `general_retrieval`: a dataset may be", "  approved for either use or both, and this tag approves no other consumer.", "  Examples:", "  past-deals-won data informing a revenue-growth client's signal judgment; a", "  person dossier informing evaluation during a manhunt operation. This", "  requires dataset-level marking, a retrieval surface the judgment layers", "  can call, and access control enforced on that retrieval (STATE", "  2026-07-14).", "", "## 5. Non-functional requirements", "", "- **NFR-1 \u2014 Scale tiers.** Day-1 target is the volume tier actually sold \u2014", "  \"a lot, not petabyte\" \u2014 with concrete numbers supplied by the", "  volume-sizing spike (DATA-1). The architecture shall reach the extreme", "  tier (petabyte-class/hour, video-dominated) through configuration and", "  fleet size alone: funnel ratios as configuration, no single-writer", "  bottleneck on any ingest path, bulk data on the S3 data plane, payloads by", "  reference. No component may require redesign to move between tiers", "  (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14). Within event synthesis, parallelism inside", "  one merge scope is governed by **declared serialization keys** (design", "  \u00a74.17; STATE 2026-07-24): the residual serial unit is the declared key", "  domain \u2014 a reviewed onboarding declaration, so tier movement stays", "  configuration \u2014 and single-lane throughput is a published capacity value", "  sized by DATA-1.", "- **NFR-2 \u2014 Government boundary & compliance.** In GovCloud deployments the", "  pipeline shall run entirely inside the boundary: FedRAMP-authorized", "  Bedrock models only, per the dated verified allowlist (FR-3.7 \u2014 errata", "  2026-07-24 removed the stale model-family ceiling from this BRD),", "  per-deployment embeddings (FR-3.8), in-boundary observability", "  (compliant-observability workstream, ENV-4), no phone-home. A Titan V2", "  retrieval-quality evaluation is a prerequisite for the first GovCloud", "  deployment (STATE 2026-07-14 embeddings strategy).", "- **NFR-3 \u2014 Lineage & access-control readiness.** 100% of accepted items", "  carry the provenance envelope and the FR-1.7 identity fields; 100% of", "  derived artifacts carry source-item lineage (FR-4.5) and write-time", "  security labels. An auditor", "  shall be able to walk from any event to its source item and markings", "  without recomputing ancestry.", "- **NFR-4 \u2014 Cost posture.** Per-item processing cost (LLM, compute, storage)", "  shall be measurable per client, feed, and stage. Infrastructure run-rate", "  per tier shall be reportable as a commercial input to package pricing", "  (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14). Extraction model tier shall be configurable", "  per client and artifact class so cheap models carry the bulk and larger", "  models are escalation, not default. Per-client, per-run metering is", "  billing-grade (FR-4.8).", "- **NFR-5 \u2014 Operability.** Worker scaling has two tiers with distinct", "  signals (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14): a thin **stream-consumer tier**", "  (validation, triage, routing \u2014 no AI calls) scales on consumer lag via", "  KEDA's Kafka-lag or CloudWatch-metric scalers, with parallelism bounded", "  by partition/shard count \u2014 partition sizing is therefore part of capacity", "  planning; **AI extraction workers** scale on SQS queue depth via KEDA,", "  the existing Datalake2 pattern. If extraction falls behind, queue depth", "  grows and absorbs the backlog: the stream is never throttled by", "  downstream AI latency. **Absorption is not sufficiency** (superseding", "  this NFR's earlier framing \u2014 STATE 2026-07-22; ingestion design \u00a74.9):", "  source-to-persist latency is governed by declared per-source **latency", "  classes** (`emergent` / `standard` / `bulk`) with per-class queue lanes", "  and priority isolation, backlog-**age** alarms against declared class", "  targets, a deterministic fast path for emergent records, and a non-LLM", "  degraded mode in which deterministic outputs keep landing while", "  model-backed stages queue without ever dropping. KEDA runs in-cluster as", "  open-source software with", "  no GovCloud availability blocker. Every stage emits throughput, latency,", "  failure, and DLQ-depth metrics; DLQ triage and replay follow runbooks on", "  the existing Event Synthesis Service model.", "- **NFR-6 \u2014 Onboarding efficiency.** A new client feed within a supported", "  modality shall be onboarded by configuration (FR-2.5) with measured", "  elapsed time (FR-2.7). Target: start at the moderate (weeks-scale) target", "  and deliberately improve toward the aggressive (days-scale) target as", "  onboarding tooling matures (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14, OD-5).", "", "## 6. Persistence architecture", "", "What technology holds the data that the analytics surface and the engines", "retrieve is the most consequential choice in this BRD. The map below is", "settled direction (STATE 2026-07-14, persistence map and open-source", "persistence mandate); the hot-store product is chosen through a structured", "bake-off (Section 6.4).", "", "### 6.1 Three stores, three jobs", "", "| Store | Holds | Serves |", "|---|---|---|", "| **Object lake** (S3-compatible) | Payloads, evidence, aged artifacts, replay history. | Reprocessing and replay, chain-of-custody evidence, archive tiers. |", "| **PostgreSQL** (Aurora in Polaris-hosted deployments; vanilla Postgres in customer-hosted) | The **system of record**: canonical events (`source_events` remain here), the engines' transactional state, entities, signals, patterns, lineage relationships, access-control enforcement (row-level security), audit records. | The engines' transactional reads and writes; the access-control floor. |", "| **Hot analytical store** | A continuously replicated (CDC-fed) **query projection** of events and extracted metadata. | Investigate Mode query tools (FR-6.3), relationship retrieval (FR-6.4), judgment-layer reference retrieval (FR-6.6), analytics. |", "", "Two rules keep the map unambiguous: **the transactional database is never", "the analytics query target, and the analytics store is never the system of", "record.**", "", "### 6.2 New artifact types and relationship edges", "", "Per-client artifact types (FR-3.5) follow the same pattern initially: a", "canonical row in PostgreSQL, a query projection in the hot store. The", "escape hatch \u2014 taken per artifact type, when a client's volume demands", "it \u2014 is to be born directly in the hot store, with only lineage stubs and", "security labels registered in PostgreSQL. In that case access control is", "enforced at the retrieval-tool layer using the security labels, because", "MySQL-dialect stores have no row-level security (STATE 2026-07-14", "persistence map).", "", "Relationship edges (FR-3.4) follow the same map: canonical rows in", "PostgreSQL like every other artifact, replicated to the hot analytical", "store with everything else (STATE 2026-07-15 relationship decision).", "", "A dedicated **graph engine is explicitly deferred**. It would be added", "only if the observed query mix shows multi-hop traversal or", "graph-algorithm demand that SQL cannot serve at acceptable latency \u2014 and", "then only as another continuously replicated projection, never a system of", "record, materialized operation-scoped first: the subgraph for a single", "`operation_id` is small, isolated, and disposable. Any engine choice is", "subject to the open-source deployability rule (Section 6.3), under which", "the credible shelf is thin (STATE 2026-07-15).", "", "### 6.3 Open-source deployability rule", "", "Every persistence dependency shall have a self-hostable open-source", "deployment path, so the same stack deploys to the Polaris cloud, GovCloud,", "or a customer-owned or air-gapped boundary. Proprietary managed services", "are acceptable only as an operational convenience over an open engine \u2014", "Aurora over Postgres, MSK over Kafka (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14", "open-source persistence mandate; exceptions require an explicit recorded", "reason). Consequences: the stream transport leans Kafka/MSK over Kinesis,", "and DynamoDB is excluded for new work.", "", "### 6.4 Hot-store selection: a structured bake-off", "", "DAT-7968 paper-screens exactly six candidates:", "", "- **TiDB** \u2014 reserved comparative hands-on slot; transactional-HTAP and", "  born-in-hot fit.", "- **StarRocks** \u2014 primary-key upserts, multi-table analytics, and direct", "  Iceberg query potential.", "- **ClickHouse** \u2014 high-throughput analytics; mutable-row, join, text, and", "  filtered-vector behavior are verify items.", "- **OpenSearch** \u2014 search-native text/vector and document-security control;", "  relational analytics and structural namespace scale are verify items.", "- **Apache Doris** \u2014 MPP SQL, mutable Unique Key/Merge-on-Write tables,", "  full-text + filtered ANN, and `VARIANT` for evolving artifacts.", "- **CrateDB** \u2014 distributed PostgreSQL-compatible SQL, BM25 + HNSW,", "  joins/aggregations, and `OBJECT(DYNAMIC)` for evolving artifacts.", "", "**Distributed PostgreSQL/Citus** with pgvector and native full-text search", "is the baseline control; **Iceberg plus a query engine** is the deep-tier", "complement. Neither can occupy a finalist slot.", "", "Finalist selection is deterministic:", "", "1. TiDB occupies one of the three hands-on slots for comparative testing.", "   The reservation is not a hard-gate waiver and does not make TiDB", "   recommendation-eligible if it fails one.", "2. Apply every pre-registered paper-screen hard gate to the other five", "   candidates. A hard-gate failure makes a challenger ineligible regardless", "   of weighted score.", "3. Advance the two eligible challengers with the highest pre-registered", "   paper-screen scores.", "4. Resolve a score tie with the pre-registered fewest-total-systems", "   tiebreaker. An unresolved tie, or fewer than two eligible challengers,", "   stops the process for an explicit product/architecture decision; a", "   failing candidate is never promoted to fill a slot.", "", "The paper screen and 2\u20133 week identical hands-on harness must prove a", "horizontally scalable, self-hosted GovCloud/EKS path; open-source", "backup/restore, upgrade, scale, and failure operations; high-rate mutable", "CDC; structural tenant/platform namespace and credential isolation; and", "security filters applied before vector/text top-k. It also tests the real", "Investigate and agent query mix over arbitrary evolving artifact shapes.", "Artifact-type metadata supplies schema, query/index, join, and reasoning", "hints to the LLM; the LLM emits a typed engine-neutral request, while", "Platform Retrieval binds the physical namespace/credential, enforces", "labels/operation/clearance, and compiles candidate-specific syntax. The", "model never supplies an arbitrary namespace, authorization predicate, SQL,", "or query fragment.", "", "Pre-registered scoring explicitly weights **text search**, the", "**transactional born-in-store scenario** from Section 6.2, metadata-guided", "agent queryability, CDC freshness/correctness, structural isolation,", "GovCloud scale/recovery, hot-window lifecycle/rebuild, and fully loaded", "system/adapter cost.", "", "**\u00a76.4 outcome (recorded 2026-08-13).**", "", "*Status: paper screen (2026-07-30) + adjudicated re-evaluation (2026-08-13)", "complete; hands-on benchmark **not run**; seat assignments below are final at", "paper stage, confirmed or moved only by the pre-registered measurement.*", "", "The re-evaluation was triggered by a corrected permission model: retrieval", "enforces exactly one row-level `audience_scope` predicate before candidate", "selection, and field-level masking is a render-time, per-customer concern \u2014", "so engine-native document/field security is not a selection differentiator.", "On the corrected weights the prior finalists tie in the mid-60s while the", "split architecture clears both by a wide, weight-insensitive margin.", "", "**The selection is an architecture with phased seats.** A **thin OpenSearch", "retrieval index** \u2014 envelope predicates (`audience_scope`, tenant, operation,", "time, type), full-text search material, embeddings, and a registry-budgeted", "set of promoted payload paths \u2014 serves every find-style query (lexical,", "vector, hybrid) with a documented guaranteed-result-count filtered-ANN", "contract and BM25 relevance. **PostgreSQL, the system of record, remains the", "payload and hydration authority for V1**: retrieval returns artifact", "identities and scores; whole artifacts, joins, and aggregations are served", "from Postgres (an isolated read projection if load requires). **ClickHouse", "(\u2265 26.3 LTS) is the designated payload engine, adopted only if a", "pre-registered measurement trigger fires** (SLO miss on the", "OpenSearch+Postgres arm, split arm clearing it with headroom); its FIPS", "posture is accepted per enclave. **Iceberg remains the deep tier.**", "Retraction is an external-versioned tombstone protocol with fail-closed", "re-authorization at hydration, so index/payload skew can only under-return,", "never leak.", "", "Eliminations re-verified against primary sources: **ClickHouse cannot hold a", "retrieval seat** (its text index provides no relevance ranking by its own", "documentation; filtered vector search concedes fewer-than-k results); **no", "single engine passes both seats** \u2014 OpenSearch's un-promoted payload tail is", "string-only with a hard field ceiling, and every update is a full-document", "re-index. **Doris** remains eliminated (ANN on the mutable table model ships", "in no release; re-screen when 4.2 ships it). **Elasticsearch** is a retrieval", "fallback pending an enclave-distribution license review; **Vespa** is", "downgraded (production Kubernetes operator is enterprise-gated);", "**Manticore** is re-opened as a bounded paper screen after its prior", "disqualifier proved stale. Full evidence: the 2026-08-13 bake-off", "adjudication record (program archive, kept outside the repo).", "", "Supporting platform policy recorded with the selection: the compatibility", "matrix now publishes a **payload structural envelope** (only", "registry-promoted paths are queryable inside retrieval; overflow is loud and", "lossless); projection policies carry **window policy classes** (7-day", "default, operation-held pinned hotness with a declared on-close", "disposition, always-hot reference corpora as priced", "elective capacity, long-window derived intelligence, short-window bulk", "evidence; hotness is declared, never usage-inferred); and **similarity is", "available across every tier at a declared latency class** (hot index,", "system-of-record pgvector lane, deep-tier exact scan), routed by Platform", "Retrieval \u2014 a capability is never silently absent for a covered time range.", "", "All hot and deep-tier reads pass the shared Platform Retrieval chokepoint;", "the model never supplies a physical namespace, credential, authorization", "predicate, or raw query fragment. Tenant-private data keeps per-tenant", "namespace and credential isolation; platform data uses a separate namespace", "and principal. This selection does not gate the V1 thin slice and does not", "implement Platform Retrieval, the production CDC rollout, or the Investigate", "Mode BRD. Hot-index footprint for elective always-hot capacity is a metered,", "billing-grade dimension (Section 7, phase 1).", "", "## 7. Phasing", "", "| Phase | Scope | Gate |", "|---|---|---|", "| **1 \u2014 Sellable core** | Text, image, and video intake and extraction (deterministic frame sampling; hosted vision models commercially, Nova-class or in-VPC vision in GovCloud); push, pull, and bulk/backfill intake; two-plane by-reference ingest with the distinct ingress identity fields (FR-1.7: `tenant_id`/`client_id`, `operation_id`, `ingest_batch_id`) and ingress payload malware scanning; agent-assisted onboarding on the propose-for-approval model with sandboxed dry-run (v1 may be engineer-driven); metadata + evidence persistence per source-type policy; billing-grade per-client metering (including hot-index footprint for elective always-hot capacity \u2014 Section 6.4 outcome); synthesis write-path scale-out foundations; events into `source_events`. | Volume numbers (DATA-1) for fleet sizing and the stream-product pick; soft-entity registry (ENT-1); GovCloud environment and LLM serving (ENV-1/ENV-3); Titan V2 retrieval-quality evaluation before the first GovCloud deployment; Nova authorization confirmation for GovCloud video; hot-store bake-off concluded (paper screen + hands-on finals \u2014 Section 6). |", "| **2 \u2014 Scale & depth** | Hot-store integration (CDC-fed query projection on the Section 6 selection); dedup quality program at volume (DATA-6); streaming entity resolution (ENT-3); full indexing surface for Investigate Mode tools; per-client artifact shapes formalized as the ontology firms up (OD-1); onboarding productized from engineer-driven sessions toward self-serve agent tooling. | Hot-store selection confirmed by the bake-off (Section 6); artifact-ontology formalization (DATA-9 / decision gate DG-3). |", "| **3 \u2014 Extreme tier (future)** | In-flight triage fleet scale-out (DATA-10); self-hosted in-VPC CV/GPU video triage at firehose scale; compute-to-data delivery via customer-boundary packaging (ENV-5) as the scaling strategy. Explicitly not day-1 (SETTLED \u2014 STATE 2026-07-14). | A customer actually buying this tier; GovCloud GPU capacity verification. |", "", "## 8. Dependencies on existing workstreams", "", "Descriptions are the substance; IDs are cross-references into the program", "workstream sheet.", "", "| Workstream | Why this BRD depends on it | Ref |", "|---|---|---|", "| Volume & requirements sizing spike | Numbers gate fleet sizing, the stream-product pick, and the cost model. | DATA-1 |", "| Durable streaming & replay architecture | Owns the two-plane intake, envelope schema, and replay contract behind FR-1.x. | DATA-2 |", "| Hot analytical store selection | Chosen through the structured bake-off (Section 6; TiDB an automatic finalist); the selected store carries the CDC-fed query projection behind FR-6.3. Part of the storage-architecture workstream. | DATA-3 |", "| Multi-modal ingestion adapters | Image/video/new-format adapter code \u2014 now day-1 scope. | DATA-4 |", "| Event-synthesis writer scale-out | FR-5.2 through FR-5.4 are its acceptance shape; implements the decided serialization contract (lanes, lease + SoR fence, per-operation identities \u2014 design \u00a74.17; STATE 2026-07-23/24). | DATA-5 |", "| Cross-source semantic dedup scale & quality | Dedup quality program over the scaled-out writer. | DATA-6 |", "| Retention & tiering policy | Constrains the per-source-type evidence policies (FR-4.2); owns who may authorize client- and operation-level destruction (FR-4.9). | DATA-7 |", "| Security markings & handling rules | Label semantics the write path stamps (FR-4.6). | DATA-8 |", "| Domain artifact ontology & schema governance | Formalizes per-client artifact shapes (FR-3.5, OD-1). | DATA-9 |", "| In-flight triage & reduction tier | Source of FR-4.1's aggregate drop accounting; hosts ingress payload malware scanning (FR-1.6); the extreme-tier funnel. | DATA-10 |", "| Soft-entity registry, person entities, entity resolution at scale | FR-3.1 prerequisites: soft entities, people, resolution machinery; entity merges must re-point relationship edges (FR-3.4). | ENT-1/2/3 |", "| GovCloud platform deployment & LLM serving | The government boundary and the Bedrock/vision-model path. | ENV-1/3 |", "| Secure software supply chain & artifact promotion | Boundary counterpart of ingress payload scanning (FR-1.6): it covers software entering the boundary; this BRD covers customer data. | ENV-6 |", "| Attribute-based access control (record-level) | Enforcement that consumes the labels this pipeline stamps. | ACC-2 |", "| End-to-end lineage (chain of custody) | The source-item identity + field-level provenance contract behind FR-4.5. | ACC-5 |", "| Real-time agentic queries over full datasets | Downstream consumer of the query surface (with Investigate Mode). | SIG-2 |", "| Mission workflows & artifact acceptance criteria | Customer inputs feeding the artifact ontology. | DISC-1 |", "", "## 9. Open decisions", "", "Two forks remain open; the product owner resolved the rest on 2026-07-14", "(resolutions table below, recorded in STATE).", "", "- **OD-1 \u2014 Artifact contract beyond events.** Formally OPEN, **DIRECTION", "  SET** (STATE 2026-07-14): each client may have its own artifact shape;", "  events remain first-class and may gain fields; non-event artifacts may", "  stay intentionally loosely typed at runtime, protected by first-class", "  platform guardrails (validation, provenance, security labels); agentic", "  system design is expected to help handle per-client shapes. Still open:", "  the exact guardrail set, schema-governance mechanics, and how loosely", "  typed artifacts participate in lineage and synthesis \u2014 owned by the domain", "  artifact ontology workstream (DATA-9) and the artifact-contract decision", "  gate (DG-3).", "- **OD-7 \u2014 Synthesis concurrency strategy. RESOLVED (STATE 2026-07-23/24).**", "  One strategy, not a per-stream menu: **serialize-by-routing** \u2014 lanes", "  keyed by the merge scope, finer by declared serialization keys (identity", "  rule), a per-lane lease with an SoR commit fence, zero duplicate canonical", "  events from concurrent resolution. Option (b), optimistic concurrency with", "  a conflict-resolution layer, was rejected (canonical-event identity churn", "  is downstream-visible); option (a)'s \"bounded duplicate tolerance\" is", "  superseded by the stronger zero-race contract. Cross-key/cross-scope", "  reconciliation is correlation-linking at the consumer layer, never", "  substrate merge or repair. Mechanics owned by DATA-5 (design \u00a74.17).", "", "| Resolved fork (from first draft) | Resolution (STATE 2026-07-14) |", "|---|---|", "| OD-2 \u2014 Control-stream transport | Settled as a shape: stream backbone plus SQS work queues for AI-processing tasks; payloads move by reference only (FR-1.3/1.4). The open-source deployability rule (Section 6) tilts the transport toward Kafka/MSK; Kinesis would serve Polaris-hosted deployments only and fork the stack across delivery models \u2014 a trade-off requiring a recorded reason. |", "| OD-3 \u2014 Evidence retention boundary | Settled: evidence/retention policy per source type, configured at client onboarding (FR-4.2). |", "| OD-4 \u2014 Onboarding agent autonomy | Settled: propose-for-approval; v1 may be an engineer driving an interactive AI session (FR-2.3). |", "| OD-5 \u2014 Onboarding time target | Settled: start at the moderate (weeks-scale) target, improve toward days-scale as tooling matures (NFR-6). |", "| OD-6 \u2014 Intake direction | Settled: both push and pull are required (FR-1.1). |", "", "## 10. References", "", "- Datalake2 Event Synthesis Service README", "  (`datalake2/src/microservices/event_synthesis/README.md`) \u2014 verified for", "  this draft: single-replica FIFO with one global message group, processing", "  ledger, create/merge/link/duplicate/ambiguous decision set, DLQ/replay", "  runbooks.", "- Accelerate models \u2014 `common/models/entities.py` (canonical-only typed-FK", "  entity bridge; no person type today) and `event_synthesis/app/models/`", "  (`source_events`, `source_event_entities`, 3072-dimension embedding", "  columns).", "- Prior cleanse-and-persist pipeline design (Jason Steen, AWS SA) \u2014 prior", "  art for the cleanse \u2192 persist flow; PGSQL-backed, storage target expected", "  to change to the three-store map (Section 6). The design artifact was not", "  available to this draft; incorporate it when the document is located."], "blocks": [{"start": 1, "end": 12, "label": "BRD \u2014 First-Party Customer Data Ingestion"}, {"start": 13, "end": 49, "label": "1. Business context & problem statement"}, {"start": 50, "end": 91, "label": "2. Goals / non-goals"}, {"start": 92, "end": 102, "label": "3. Personas & consumers"}, {"start": 103, "end": 445, "label": "4. Functional requirements"}, {"start": 446, "end": 507, "label": "5. Non-functional requirements"}, {"start": 508, "end": 681, "label": "6. Persistence architecture"}, {"start": 682, "end": 689, "label": "7. Phasing"}, {"start": 690, "end": 714, "label": "8. Dependencies on existing workstreams"}, {"start": 715, "end": 748, "label": "9. Open decisions"}, {"start": 749, "end": 763, "label": "10. References"}], "lineCount": 763, "sha256": "5802fd5d265f06f99e0e777e268fc7f34691c4467185705b3967a35bcf78b3ca", "endsWithNewline": true});
